00:01:01.913 --> 00:01:04.890
Test one, AI headshots.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.600
Turns out a lot of people want some free

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.610
professional shots for their.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:09.750
- It's going on the LinkedIn.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.550
- I might have a new LinkedIn photo.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.685
- [Host] So instead of hiring
a professional photographer,

00:01:13.685 --> 00:01:16.140
makeup, hair, and a stylist,

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:20.352
these folks stepped into my
very professional photo studio.

00:01:20.352 --> 00:01:21.780
- Nice catch.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.550
- Get my lens clean a little bit here.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.450
You're very upset.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.010
You hate me.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:26.843
Perfect.

00:01:26.843 --> 00:01:28.067
Smize.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.100
- I don't know what that is?

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.423
- Smiling with your eyes.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.700
And I used a generative AI
headshot tool called Try It On.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.460
Here's how it works, you
upload 10 or more photos

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.110
to Try It On's website.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.630
In this case, I'm using Jordan's photos.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.270
And then you select the
types of shots you'd like,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.900
business office, business
studio, business outdoors.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.073
So much business.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:54.000
The photos are then used
to train an AI model.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.740
That model learns what you look like,

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.630
the size of your eyes, your nose,

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.940
your other facial attributes.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.910
Then once it learns it, it
looks at a library of images

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.430
it already has learned from and says this

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:09.090
is what Jordan looks like in
a blue suit or in a Navy suit.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.880
For $17, you get a hundred images .

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.800
For every batch, I found
that there were around

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.340
five to seven images that
really looked like the subject.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.560
- That's incredible, AI is real.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.000
- That's nice.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.980
Very mysterious, huh?

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.470
- [Host] Others were just hilariously bad.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.814
- Those teeth are a little creepy there.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:28.647
(bell ticking)

00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:29.850
- Those teeth are a lot of teeth.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:30.683
- That's a lot.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.580
It might be more than
humanly possible to have.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.150
- Test two, AI extreme makeover.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.640
- I would be the pretty witch.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:39.473
- Harry Potter.

00:02:39.473 --> 00:02:41.370
- CNN's Top anchor.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:44.765
- Okay, yeah, sometimes people
really want to bend reality

00:02:44.765 --> 00:02:46.710
and with a tool like Midjourney,

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:50.970
real photo portraits can
go from this, to this.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.400
Unfortunately, for people
who want that kind of result,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.590
Midjourney is a bit complicated.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:58.590
It runs through Discord,
a popular chat app.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:02:59.940
After you've signed up, you type

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.073
in a prompt describing the image you want.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:06.300
My producer, Kenny has
become a pro at this.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.510
In these cases, Kenny
used a two-step process.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.540
First, he created the scenes
that people wanted to be in.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.300
Then he used a Midjourney
tool called Insight Face Swap

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.363
to get the subject's
faces into the images.

00:03:19.975 --> 00:03:20.940
All right, ready?

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:21.773
- Ready.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:26.130
Well, this is what future
Me is gonna look like.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.420
- Amazing.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.410
- Big reveal.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.400
- Big reveal.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.910
- I like that, now this one I like.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.440
I look like a true wizard.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.633
- Test three, AI editing.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.700
Sometimes people just want
something very specific.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.860
So what kind of photo
would you like today?

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.030
- I would like a photo

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.830
of myself professionally in a white coat.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.000
- Why a white coat?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.880
- So I'm a doctor and we
obviously take headshots whenever

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.320
we go to new hospital, and I want to see

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.900
if this one can beat my real one.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.540
- So, we took a few photos of
Joe and plugged the best one

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.900
into Adobe's new Firefly
generative fill tool.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.850
I clicked the background
button and replaced it

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:05.910
with an AI generated image of a library.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.260
Then I erased his outfit

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.133
and told it to generate
a white doctor's coat.

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:13.662
Okay, so he sorta looks like
a doctor from a board game

00:04:13.662 --> 00:04:17.880
but maybe it could pass
us as new profile photo.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:18.713
These sorts

00:04:18.713 --> 00:04:21.990
of changes were once the
stuff of Photoshop masters.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.720
But now with AI, it's so simple.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.450
With Magic Eraser integrated
into Google Photos

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.781
you can quickly remove
things in the background.

00:04:29.781 --> 00:04:31.230
And with Face App,

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:34.200
you can change hair color,
add facial expressions

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.880
or glasses.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.640
So what did we learn here today?

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.457
Well, that photography
will never be the same.

00:04:41.457 --> 00:04:46.080
Yes, these tools are fun, but
they can also be not so fun.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.620
What about real photographers and artists?

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.250
I was able to set up shop here

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.960
with just some basic tech tools

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.270
and make some compelling art.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.940
Then how will we know
the real from the fake

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:01.050
especially with photos of people
in compromising situations?

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.010
One sign of hope,

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.800
when I saved this photo
in Adobe Firefly it baked

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.464
in information to the file about
how it was created with AI.

00:05:08.464 --> 00:05:12.060
Adobe is hoping media, tech
and social media platforms

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:15.030
will make it easy to see that information.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.260
Until then, good luck
telling the real from the AI,

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.210
especially on LinkedIn.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.940
You could be helped by AI.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.790
Just joking, you're a natural beauty.

